   115	def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
   116	    """
   117	    Rebuild the dense pattern whose transformed even-even subsample matches the sparse dot board.
   118	
   119	    Input structure:
   120	    - The grid is partitioned by full-background separator bands into equal odd square panels.
   121	    - Exactly one panel is a sparse dot lattice: only even-row/even-column cells may be colored, and all other cells are background.
   122	    - The remaining panels are dense multicolor candidate boards shown in their original poses.
   123	
   124	    Rule:
   125	    - Find the unique candidate and unique pose among the 8 allowed poses: rotate by 0/90/180/270 degrees, or mirror left-right first and then rotate.
   126	    - For each candidate pose, compare the whole sparse projection obtained by keeping only even-row/even-column cells and setting every other cell to background.
   127	    - Exactly one posed candidate matches the dot panel at every sampled position, including sampled background cells.
   128	    - Output that candidate in the matching pose as a full dense board.
   129	
   130	    Key insight:
   131	    - The sparse panel is not the answer itself; it is a downsampled projection that jointly reveals both which candidate to use and which pose to apply.
   132	    """
